1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,080
[A mass collapse at Minshin Road
is suspected to have caused an outbreak]

2
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,800
[It was a week ago
at Minshin Road, Taipei,]

3
00:00:01,890 --> 00:00:03,780
[when the mass collapse occurred.]

4
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:04,750
[Similar cases have been reported]

5
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:06,810
[all across Taiwan.]

6
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,100
[It's suspected to be]

7
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:11,170
[a new type of infectious disease.]

8
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,240
[We have exclusive information.]

9
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:14,160
[Across Taiwan,]

10
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:16,410
[the patients who fainted for no reason]

11
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:17,680
[were found to have]

12
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:20,010
[an unknown whitish algae
in their bodies.]

13
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,390
[Meanwhile, the same algae was found]

14
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:23,930
[on patients who tragically passed away,]

15
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:25,690
[covering all of the body's organs,]

16
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:28,510
[causing multiple organ failures.]

17
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:30,970
[Based on clinical observations,]

18
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,600
[the whitish algae is the key reason]

19
00:00:32,729 --> 00:00:34,580
[that causes
the unreasonable mass collapse.]

20
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:37,480
[But the whitish algae]

21
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:39,550
[doesn't belong]

22
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,220
[to any known type of algae
found on Earth.]

23
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:42,850
[We've also yet to determine]

24
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:46,020
[the means of transmission.]

25
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:47,290
[Breaking news.]

26
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,350
[Just a moment ago,]

27
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,110
[a restaurant in Yangmingshan]

28
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,090
[faced another occurrence
of mass collapse.]

29
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,670
[Dozens of people
were rushed to the hospital.]

30
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,210
[Since it's the flowering season,]

31
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:56,530
[many tourists are visiting the mountain.]

32
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:57,720
[Thus, a large-scale outbreak]

33
00:00:57,810 --> 00:00:59,700
[is highly possible.]

34
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:01,550
[The national park has decided
to close off the mountain temporarily.]

35
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,480
[The Centers for Disease Control
and Prevention has also given a name]

36
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:04,940
[to this unknown disease,]

37
00:01:05,019 --> 00:01:07,530
[which is the White Algae Disorder.]

38
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:09,160
[Yung-kang.]

39
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:09,380
[Let me ask you a simple question.]

40
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:11,760
[Many conflicting opinions
on where the disease came from]

41
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,300
[How does alga]

42
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:14,920
[keep itself alive?]

43
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:16,020
[It needs water.]

44
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:18,440
[That's right, water.]

45
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:19,590
[But think about it.]

46
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:20,950
[When was the last time
it rained in Taiwan?]

47
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:21,130
[Many conflicting opinions
on where the disease came from]

48
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:22,140
[It has been a long time ago.]

49
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:23,550
[If the plum rain still won't come,]

50
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,960
[all our reservoirs will be empty.]

51
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:26,360
[So...]

52
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:27,510
[while Taiwan is currently facing]

53
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:30,150
[a severe shortage of water,]

54
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:32,000
[the algae has to find a place]

55
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:35,030
[that is moist in order to survive.]

56
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,090
[It needs to survive.]

57
00:01:36,170 --> 00:01:36,220
[Think about it, a hydrated place]

58
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:38,590
[Many conflicting opinions
on where the disease came from]

59
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,530
[where 70% is made up of water.]

60
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:41,810
[Where is it?]

61
00:01:41,890 --> 00:01:43,350
[Hold on.]

62
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,900
[Are you making a connection between that]

63
00:01:46,030 --> 00:01:47,039
[and the White Algae Disorder?]

64
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:49,110
[The human body contains 70% of water.]

65
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,750
[So the lack of rain]

66
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,590
[caused the algae]

67
00:01:52,670 --> 00:01:53,770
[to attach to human bodies.]

68
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:54,130
[Is that what you mean?]

69
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:54,700
[A lack of water sources caused algae
to parasitize human body?]

70
00:01:54,789 --> 00:01:56,280
[That's right, Yung-kang.]

71
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:57,430
[Think about it.]

72
00:01:57,509 --> 00:01:59,670
[What's the origin of life?]

73
00:01:59,759 --> 00:02:01,120
[It's water, isn't it?]

74
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:02,710
[A billion years ago,]

75
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,860
[lightning struck the sea.]

76
00:02:04,990 --> 00:02:06,010
[Suddenly,]

77
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:07,500
[life was created.]

78
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:09,389
[What was the first form of life?]

79
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:11,420
[It's algae.]

80
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:13,490
[So every creature on Earth]

81
00:02:13,570 --> 00:02:14,540
[can't survive]

82
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:16,300
[without water.]

83
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:19,470
[Now, it has flipped on its head]

84
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,579
[and it's bringing death to us all.]

85
00:02:21,670 --> 00:02:22,990
[Before, algae brought life]

86
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,570
[to Earth and humans.]

87
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:25,890
[Based on your logic,]

88
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,000
[it's now going to take life away.]

89
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:29,540
[Isn't that pointing
to the end of humanity?]

90
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:29,720
[That's right.]

91
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,130
[The Earth's comeback,
White Algae Disease is a toll of doom]

92
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,760
[So now,]

93
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:34,079
[you and I,]

94
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:36,190
[and all the viewers
watching our program,]

95
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,390
[would like to ask a question.]

96
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:42,130
[Do you think this is a warning from God?]

97
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:43,320
[During this time,]

98
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,500
[shouldn't we humans do something]

99
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:46,970
[in response to God's warning?]

100
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:48,160
[The Earth's comeback,
White Algae Disease is a toll of doom]

101
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,480
[Based on your assessment,]

102
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,060
[we really need to reflect
on this matter.]

103
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:53,130
[Could this be Earth's comeback]

104
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,020
[as well as a warning from God?]

105
00:02:55,110 --> 00:02:57,790
[Perhaps it's going to end]

106
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,380
[the way it started.]

107
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:43,810
Let's bid for this one.

108
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,010
[Mountain Travel, a journey of the heart]

109
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:47,990
We'll conduct a training course

110
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:49,620
to help new tour guides

111
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:51,290
prepare for the qualification.

112
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:54,860
Mom, we've never bid on those.

113
00:03:54,950 --> 00:03:56,570
Are you sure this will work?

114
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:58,070
We'll just have to make sure we get it.

115
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:00,000
Otherwise, all the trips this year
have been canceled.

116
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:02,600
We need to make money for the company.

117
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,700
What about this?

118
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:09,110
This looks good.

119
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:12,940
We can use the yearly schedule
in our tourist guide.

120
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,360
It's not bad.

121
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,700
It also suits Pu's expertise.

122
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:20,019
We can discuss it with him

123
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:21,740
once he's discharged.

124
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,260
He's a terrible photographer.

125
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:28,430
But it's okay.

126
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:29,970
Once he's discharged,

127
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:31,460
I'll keep an eye on him.

128
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:33,840
Ting-yi, help me check

129
00:04:33,930 --> 00:04:34,940
if there are any specifications

130
00:04:35,030 --> 00:04:36,520
we have to adhere to
for the bidding proposal.

131
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:36,740
[Mountain Travel, a journey of the heart]

132
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:37,840
The three of us can brainstorm

133
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,080
on other ideas.

134
00:04:39,159 --> 00:04:40,570
Okay.

135
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,610
Have you heard of a company

136
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,500
called New World Horizon?

137
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:54,470
The boss is called Mr. Sung Hsiao-feng.
There is also...

138
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,400
Who?

139
00:04:59,670 --> 00:05:01,730
Did you get in touch with a new company?

140
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:04,370
Or did you help us get a new client?

141
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:09,610
No, I'm just asking

142
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:12,070
if you've heard of it.

143
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:14,710
Vacation planning

144
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,830
is the trend these days.

145
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:19,950
So I thought I could get in touch

146
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,360
with this company.

147
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:23,030
Sure, go ahead.

148
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,540
We'll discuss it again
if there's any potential.

149
00:05:25,630 --> 00:05:26,640
Okay.

150
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,990
Let me see that folder.

151
00:05:31,130 --> 00:05:31,870
Here.

152
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:32,490
Yes.

153
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:35,170
So Ms. Chang-fen and the others' memories

154
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:36,840
have been modified?

155
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:40,940
When I went to your office two days ago,

156
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,310
Fali had already modified

157
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:45,290
all of your colleagues' memories.

158
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:48,060
They don't know me or Fali anymore.

159
00:05:48,590 --> 00:05:50,000
It's as if

160
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,380
we've never appeared at your company.

161
00:05:53,610 --> 00:05:55,240
Why would Fali do that?

162
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:02,800
Almighty Shennong, God of Five Grains.

163
00:06:02,890 --> 00:06:04,520
[Lead the way]

164
00:06:04,610 --> 00:06:06,100
[Smooth sailing]

165
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:15,040
A magical method for purifying the mind.

166
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:20,490
Pray reverently
and the light shall shine on you.

167
00:06:27,930 --> 00:06:28,890
These humans...

168
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:32,550
All the Kawas have retreated.

169
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:34,350
There are no more Kawas in this world,

170
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,510
so praying is useless.

171
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:40,159
How did it go? Have you seen Fali?

172
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:42,530
He hasn't shown up

173
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,120
since Tien-ti had that dream.

174
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:46,890
Maybe you could use the Reflection of Time

175
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:48,520
to find out where he might be.

176
00:06:49,310 --> 00:06:50,980
Apart from the Reflection of Time
of the doomsday,

177
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:52,430
I saw nothing else.

178
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:56,350
How could that be?

179
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:57,710
I don't know.

180
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:01,810
Regarding the Reflection of Time

181
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:03,740
and Fali,

182
00:07:04,010 --> 00:07:05,720
Toem, that wretched woman

183
00:07:05,850 --> 00:07:07,970
who told me not to trust Fali,

184
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:10,520
and Papa' orip with the white footprints,

185
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:14,170
everything is out of control

186
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:15,880
just like this world.

187
00:07:18,170 --> 00:07:20,990
Seriously, if my wife were still here

188
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,000
to see all this chaos

189
00:07:22,090 --> 00:07:23,630
and uncertainties,

190
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,120
it would surely have made her explode.

191
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:27,150
I would have been blown up too.

192
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,390
When your wife was helping Fali

193
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:31,550
to evacuate all the Kawas,

194
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:34,760
did she mention anything weird

195
00:07:34,850 --> 00:07:35,950
about Fali?

196
00:07:44,090 --> 00:07:45,940
How could I remember?

197
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:46,990
Whenever my wife spoke,

198
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,900
it always came in one ear
and out the other.

199
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:54,080
Especially if it was about work.

200
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,710
I paid no attention at all.

201
00:08:02,790 --> 00:08:04,550
Don't look at me like that.

202
00:08:16,210 --> 00:08:18,580
[If Fali is really up to something]

203
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:20,210
[like what 'Orad said...]

204
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,270
My goodness.

205
00:08:26,190 --> 00:08:28,610
My wife worked for him for so long.

206
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:30,860
She was so loyal to him
and obeyed all his directives.

207
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:35,169
Don't tell me that she and Fali
are keeping something from 'Orad.

208
00:08:36,669 --> 00:08:38,120
That's not good.

209
00:08:38,210 --> 00:08:39,700
It's not like she doesn't know

210
00:08:39,789 --> 00:08:41,950
that 'Orad is the messenger of Kakarayan.

211
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:44,500
Keeping it from 'Orad is the same
as keeping it from Kakarayan.

212
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:46,080
My goodness.

213
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:47,660
Honey, you can't be that stupid

214
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,950
to go against Kakarayan, right?

215
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,930
Yes. 'Orad and I are close.

216
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:53,340
That's true.

217
00:08:53,430 --> 00:08:55,280
But you can't lie to him like this.

218
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:59,240
Honey, you can't be that stupid.

219
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:02,050
You're the wife of the god of wisdom.

220
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:13,180
What a mess.

221
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:17,940
I would've been beaten to death
if I were home.

222
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:25,330
Honey.

223
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:26,960
If you were here,

224
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:28,320
you'd never let this place look like this.

225
00:09:28,410 --> 00:09:29,730
Am I right?

226
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:31,130
It wouldn't be messy like this.

227
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:32,670
Am I right?

228
00:09:33,910 --> 00:09:36,060
I only haven't been here for a week.

229
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:36,940
But your lab

230
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:38,790
has turned into a garbage dump again.

231
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:40,730
And how many times have I told you?

232
00:09:40,810 --> 00:09:43,450
The books should be arranged
according to height.

233
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:45,920
Honey, listen to me.

234
00:09:46,050 --> 00:09:48,340
I've studied psychology.

235
00:09:48,470 --> 00:09:49,970
Our speech and actions

236
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:52,470
are affected by the subconscious mind.

237
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,320
My lab is this messy

238
00:09:54,410 --> 00:09:56,130
because subconsciously,

239
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:57,800
I need you.

240
00:09:57,890 --> 00:10:00,000
I need to see my dear wife all the time.

241
00:10:00,090 --> 00:10:00,830
Nonsense.

242
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,900
You're just lazy.

243
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:08,580
It's not nonsense.

244
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:11,000
I've been really busy lately.

245
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:13,460
Humans won't stop creating
a bunch of cause and effect.

246
00:10:13,810 --> 00:10:15,840
Why bother with social media apps?

247
00:10:15,930 --> 00:10:18,390
Someone pressed like,
someone is following someone.

248
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,720
Someone posted
something accessible to so and so.

249
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:23,620
All these causes and effects
will be recorded.

250
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:26,040
I already have enough on my plate.

251
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:28,550
Then leave me alone.

252
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,000
How can I leave you alone?

253
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:39,600
Honey.

254
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,340
You don't seem like yourself today.

255
00:10:44,350 --> 00:10:46,590
Is there something you want to tell me?

256
00:10:52,090 --> 00:10:53,850
I got it.

257
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,300
Don't be mad.

258
00:10:55,390 --> 00:10:56,360
Relax.

259
00:10:56,490 --> 00:10:57,590
Take a deep breath.

260
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,130
Although I don't know what I did wrong...

261
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,210
You're a professor

262
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:03,800
and your lab is a mess.

263
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:05,730
What would the other professors
and students think

264
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:06,740
when they walk in?

265
00:11:09,430 --> 00:11:12,370
It's okay. We have to learn to grow up.

266
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,850
I can tidy things up without you.

267
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:18,710
Why is it harder than it looks?

268
00:11:20,950 --> 00:11:23,370
I really can't tidy things up without you.

269
00:11:27,550 --> 00:11:29,450
Why did you have to go back to Pinokayan?

270
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:31,870
Isn't it better to stay here with me?

271
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:38,510
[Honey.]

272
00:11:39,430 --> 00:11:40,710
What do you think

273
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,650
Pinokayan is like?

274
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:44,930
We'll be there soon.

275
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:45,770
You'll see then.

276
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:46,650
Why are you asking about it?

277
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:49,550
Don't you think it's amazing?

278
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,490
It's called the "homeland."

279
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:52,850
We're going home.

280
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:54,660
But logically speaking,

281
00:11:54,740 --> 00:11:57,300
home is where you were born and raised.

282
00:11:57,650 --> 00:11:58,880
From the very beginning,

283
00:11:59,010 --> 00:11:59,980
Kawas have been living with humans.

284
00:12:00,110 --> 00:12:01,650
This is our home.

285
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,710
And I've never heard of anyone

286
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:04,030
who came from Pinokayan.

287
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:06,840
You're talking nonsense

288
00:12:06,930 --> 00:12:08,740
because you don't want to go back, right?

289
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:10,360
No.

290
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,420
Kakarayan had told us

291
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:14,020
why we have to go back.

292
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,260
Yes.

293
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:17,490
Because He said

294
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:19,560
that He would take back
all the blessings of the world.

295
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,140
Sometimes, I think Kawas like you

296
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:25,590
are so strange.

297
00:12:25,810 --> 00:12:26,780
From beginning to end,

298
00:12:26,910 --> 00:12:28,180
no one has ever seen him in person.

299
00:12:28,270 --> 00:12:29,110
But you make it sound like

300
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,780
Kakarayan spoke to you face-to-face.

301
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:32,630
What do you mean by Kawas like me?

302
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,300
Aren't you a Kawas too?

303
00:12:35,710 --> 00:12:36,760
You'd better watch what you say.

304
00:12:36,850 --> 00:12:37,820
What if Kakarayan

305
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:39,580
punishes you when you return?

306
00:12:40,330 --> 00:12:41,510
You'll save me, won't you?

307
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:03,500
Banai.

308
00:15:10,050 --> 00:15:11,060
What brings you here?

309
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:18,540
Where's Tien-ti?

310
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:22,280
Neither Tien-ti nor the messenger is here.

311
00:15:22,370 --> 00:15:23,690
This time, it's just me.

312
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:27,120
I need your help with something.

313
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,410
I'm looking for a Kawas.

314
00:15:29,810 --> 00:15:31,520
I need you to help me
with the Ceremony of Connection.

315
00:15:33,590 --> 00:15:35,920
All the Kawas are gone.

316
00:15:37,290 --> 00:15:39,270
I'm no longer a Sikawasay.

317
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,610
I can't help you.

318
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:47,450
Don't worry. I know every Sikawasay

319
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:49,040
has his or her own master.

320
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,360
So this time,

321
00:15:50,490 --> 00:15:52,200
let me be your master temporarily.

322
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,060
I know I'm not as powerful

323
00:15:55,150 --> 00:15:56,820
as the messenger of Kakarayan
or other Kawas.

324
00:15:56,910 --> 00:15:59,070
I can't cure sickness and such things.

325
00:15:59,150 --> 00:16:00,520
Nevertheless,

326
00:16:00,610 --> 00:16:02,060
I'm still a Kawas.

327
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:03,070
So conducting the Ceremony of Connection

328
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:04,610
shouldn't be a problem.

329
00:16:12,090 --> 00:16:13,810
Please help me, Banai.

330
00:16:13,890 --> 00:16:15,740
You're the only one who can help me.

331
00:16:16,310 --> 00:16:17,370
Let me be honest with you.

332
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:18,210
Since all the Kawas

333
00:16:18,290 --> 00:16:20,050
retreated that day,

334
00:16:20,450 --> 00:16:22,170
something just doesn't feel right.

335
00:16:22,250 --> 00:16:23,350
But I can't say what it is.

336
00:16:23,490 --> 00:16:24,760
I don't know
if anybody else is feeling it.

337
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:26,610
But have you ever thought about this,
Banai?

338
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:27,890
Could it be

339
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:29,380
that the place the Kawas went to

340
00:16:29,470 --> 00:16:31,100
was not Pinokayan after all?

341
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:48,040
This is all just my speculation though.

342
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:49,710
I need you

343
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,950
to help me conduct
the Ceremony of Connection

344
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:52,880
so that I can verify

345
00:16:53,010 --> 00:16:54,770
whether or not my assumption is true.

346
00:17:02,070 --> 00:17:03,880
Which Kawas are you looking for?

347
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,040
I'm looking for my wife,

348
00:17:08,010 --> 00:17:09,240
Malusakadat.

349
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:31,020
♫ I can't see you, but I know ♫

350
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:38,330
♫ The sky is clear after the rain,
reminding me to be well ♫

351
00:17:38,410 --> 00:17:44,130
♫ A silent prayer,
wanting no interruptions ♫

352
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:52,360
♫ How nice would it be
if we could meet again? ♫

353
00:17:52,850 --> 00:17:56,540
♫ Come on, come on ♫

354
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:59,800
♫ Let me hear you ♫

355
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:03,270
♫ Come on, come on ♫

356
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:06,710
♫ Let me see you ♫

357
00:18:06,930 --> 00:18:10,490
♫ Come on, come on ♫

358
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:20,830
♫ Right at this moment,
show yourself before me ♫

359
00:18:25,010 --> 00:18:25,980
It's not like that, my beautiful wife.

360
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,380
I've completely discarded

361
00:18:27,470 --> 00:18:28,350
that thought.

362
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,360
It's true. You have to believe me.

363
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:30,550
I assure you there is none.

364
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,480
Now, when I think

365
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:32,840
of going back to Pinokayan,

366
00:18:32,930 --> 00:18:36,230
I feel so happy that I can't wait.

367
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:38,120
Li Pu-hui.

368
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:39,840
Where is your necklace?

369
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,200
I think I lost it.

370
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:42,700
You lost it?

371
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:45,160
How could you lose something so important?

372
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:12,260
How was it, Banai?

373
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,630
Did you see my wife?

374
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:23,040
So where is she now?

375
00:19:25,510 --> 00:19:26,430
The platform.

376
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,840
I saw you standing on the platform

377
00:19:32,630 --> 00:19:34,880
where the Kawas were preparing to leave.

378
00:19:35,710 --> 00:19:38,130
You two were talking on the platform.

379
00:19:40,070 --> 00:19:41,300
But it was too far.

380
00:19:42,750 --> 00:19:43,900
I couldn't hear you.

381
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:46,800
Then both of you disappeared.

382
00:19:50,190 --> 00:19:51,070
That was it?

383
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:53,530
I disappeared

384
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,160
and so did my wife?

385
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:58,500
But where did she go?

386
00:19:59,250 --> 00:20:00,790
Banai, think again.

387
00:20:00,970 --> 00:20:02,640
Did you see anything else?

388
00:20:06,420 --> 00:20:07,700
A suitcase.

389
00:20:10,470 --> 00:20:13,600
I saw a suitcase on the platform.

390
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:34,060
Are you going to see Sung-en?

391
00:20:38,630 --> 00:20:39,600
Don't go.

392
00:20:42,150 --> 00:20:43,820
This is completely pointless.

393
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,640
What do you mean by completely pointless?

394
00:20:52,970 --> 00:20:55,310
Sure, it's completely pointless to you.

395
00:20:57,810 --> 00:20:59,000
I know that meeting Sung-en

396
00:20:59,090 --> 00:21:00,890
won't make her get better.

397
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:02,960
I know that no matter
how many times I visit her,

398
00:21:03,090 --> 00:21:03,930
I can't change your mind

399
00:21:04,020 --> 00:21:05,560
about not wanting to save her.

400
00:21:07,450 --> 00:21:08,950
Because of Fali,

401
00:21:09,030 --> 00:21:11,230
Sung-en could very well
have forgotten about me.

402
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:13,350
But that doesn't mean

403
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:15,630
I can pretend that nothing happened.

404
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:17,920
Because you could have changed it.

405
00:21:18,890 --> 00:21:20,340
But I couldn't persuade you.

406
00:21:22,370 --> 00:21:24,080
It's because you saw that I was alive

407
00:21:24,170 --> 00:21:25,360
in the Reflection of Time,

408
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:27,250
you decided to let everyone die.

409
00:21:27,340 --> 00:21:28,440
I'm telling you not to go

410
00:21:29,230 --> 00:21:31,690
because she passed away a few days ago.

411
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:38,340
Sung-en is dead?

412
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:40,010
Yes.

413
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,130
The day after you went to see her

414
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,800
on the night of the surgery.

415
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:48,370
So you knew this was going to happen,

416
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:49,910
but you still didn't tell me.

417
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,270
I told you.

418
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:53,080
Whether Sung-en lives or dies

419
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,530
has nothing to do with you.

420
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:56,820
So whether I like it or not,

421
00:21:56,950 --> 00:21:58,710
as long as I stay alive

422
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,640
and as long as you can continue
to protect me,

423
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:03,590
you don't care what happens

424
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:05,400
to Sung-en, Pu,

425
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:06,630
or anyone else around me?

426
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:07,290
Yes.

427
00:22:08,390 --> 00:22:09,840
As long as you live,

428
00:22:09,930 --> 00:22:11,860
I don't care about others.

429
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:13,890
Have you ever thought about it?

430
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:16,220
If the people around me

431
00:22:16,310 --> 00:22:17,710
disappear one by one

432
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:19,170
and I'm the only one that's left,

433
00:22:19,300 --> 00:22:20,710
what's the point in living?

434
00:22:23,610 --> 00:22:24,710
In that case,

435
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:26,870
I don't even want to have a choice.

436
00:22:27,570 --> 00:22:29,950
I don't want to know about doomsday.

437
00:22:30,560 --> 00:22:32,450
I don't want to know about the Kawas

438
00:22:32,590 --> 00:22:34,480
and I don't want to remember you!

439
00:22:53,130 --> 00:22:54,410
[Thank you, Banai.]

440
00:22:55,470 --> 00:22:56,520
There's one more thing

441
00:22:56,610 --> 00:22:58,330
I need to ask from you.

442
00:22:58,410 --> 00:23:00,040
It's about me coming here.

443
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:01,490
Please don't let Tien-ti

444
00:23:01,620 --> 00:23:03,560
or the messenger of Kakarayan know.

445
00:23:05,890 --> 00:23:06,950
Because the whole thing

446
00:23:07,080 --> 00:23:08,970
is more complicated than I thought.

447
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:10,910
I'm afraid if they find out,

448
00:23:12,490 --> 00:23:14,080
Tien-ti will be in trouble.

449
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:32,910
[Hualien]

450
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,210
Ma'am.

451
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:18,750
Do you need any help?

452
00:24:21,310 --> 00:24:23,290
Where is the exit?

453
00:24:24,780 --> 00:24:25,880
Where are you going?

454
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:28,920
The bus stop.

455
00:24:29,230 --> 00:24:32,440
If it's the bus stop,
it should be upstairs.

456
00:24:32,530 --> 00:24:34,590
There should be a sign showing the way.

457
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,470
Is it from there?

458
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:37,190
Yes, there's a signboard over there.

459
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:38,380
Why don't I...

460
00:24:38,510 --> 00:24:39,170
I'm heading there too. I'll show you.

461
00:24:39,260 --> 00:24:41,850
Someone passed out!

462
00:24:43,350 --> 00:24:44,490
What's wrong with him?

463
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:47,350
Someone, call for help!

464
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:50,740
Do you know CPR? Let's take turns.

465
00:24:50,830 --> 00:24:51,930
I can do it.

466
00:26:02,630 --> 00:26:05,360
[I don't want to know about doomsday.]

467
00:26:05,670 --> 00:26:07,520
I don't want to know about the Kawas

468
00:26:07,610 --> 00:26:09,150
and I don't want to remember you!

469
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:34,140
[Do you even know how to ride a bike?]

470
00:26:34,220 --> 00:26:35,240
It's not my fault!

471
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:37,130
That kid suddenly ran out.

472
00:26:37,260 --> 00:26:39,200
That's why I stopped, okay?

473
00:27:16,810 --> 00:27:17,870
Yi-han.

474
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:20,070
Why are you doing the newsletter?

475
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:21,790
Isn't that Pu's job?

476
00:27:23,550 --> 00:27:26,930
Yes. I don't know how to design it,

477
00:27:27,330 --> 00:27:29,880
but I can help with the editorial content.

478
00:27:32,350 --> 00:27:35,780
You're working on someone else's job.
This isn't like you.

479
00:27:39,740 --> 00:27:42,070
I wonder when Pu will be back.

480
00:27:47,610 --> 00:27:48,270
Right.

481
00:27:48,620 --> 00:27:49,770
The print shop called to say

482
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:51,180
the DM for the copy is ready.

483
00:27:51,260 --> 00:27:52,320
I have to go get it.

484
00:27:53,730 --> 00:27:55,750
But I haven't finished
my editorial commentary yet.

485
00:27:56,590 --> 00:27:58,390
And I haven't sorted the photos
from my camera yet.

486
00:27:58,480 --> 00:27:59,140
Wu Yi-han.

487
00:27:59,760 --> 00:28:01,250
Go finish your work. I'll get it for you.

488
00:28:01,340 --> 00:28:04,240
Let's go through the photos now.

489
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:05,210
Come on.

490
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:18,590
[Mountain Travel. Let's get through 2021!]

491
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:47,850
[If the people around me]

492
00:28:47,980 --> 00:28:49,390
[disappear one by one]

493
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:50,930
[and I'm the only one that's left,]

494
00:28:51,010 --> 00:28:52,600
[what's the point in living?]

495
00:29:36,860 --> 00:29:41,080
[2025, Unrest in many European countries
due to dispute over water sources]

496
00:29:42,270 --> 00:29:43,460
That's strange.

497
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:47,460
The future hasn't changed.

498
00:30:23,230 --> 00:30:24,110
Are you okay?

499
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:28,120
We have to go back now. Hurry!

500
00:30:28,250 --> 00:30:29,350
Wu Yi-han and Ting-yi are in the office.

501
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:30,580
Didn't you see?

502
00:30:30,710 --> 00:30:32,080
He obviously came for you.

503
00:30:32,170 --> 00:30:33,400
I can't let you go back.

504
00:30:33,490 --> 00:30:35,770
We can't leave them like that. I...

505
00:30:38,990 --> 00:30:40,750
Tell me.

506
00:30:40,830 --> 00:30:42,590
Who am I?

507
00:30:44,180 --> 00:30:46,070
Why?

508
00:30:46,160 --> 00:30:47,300
Why?

509
00:30:47,430 --> 00:30:49,060
Why am I always alone?

510
00:30:50,600 --> 00:30:51,830
Grandma!

511
00:31:08,460 --> 00:31:09,830
[Please, just this once.]

512
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:10,710
[Next episode]

513
00:31:10,800 --> 00:31:12,420
[Let me see my grandma today.]

514
00:31:12,510 --> 00:31:13,660
[Your grandma]

515
00:31:13,740 --> 00:31:15,370
[might not live through the day.]

516
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:17,180
[My dear wife.]

517
00:31:17,260 --> 00:31:19,020
[You never leave anything behind.]

518
00:31:19,110 --> 00:31:20,920
[Why did you leave your suitcase]

519
00:31:21,310 --> 00:31:22,590
[and then leave?]

520
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:24,700
[Everything we believed to be true]

521
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:27,340
[might just be a lie someone made up.]

522
00:31:27,600 --> 00:31:28,880
[Kakarayan.]

523
00:31:29,010 --> 00:31:31,430
[I know you can save my grandma.]

524
00:31:31,650 --> 00:31:33,940
[I'm the one you've been calling out to.]

525
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:35,700
[I'm the one you've been looking for.]

526
00:31:36,230 --> 00:31:38,560
[The beginning and the end of everything.]

527
00:31:40,060 --> 00:31:51,100
[Goodbye]

528
00:32:17,190 --> 00:32:19,390
So this is what the sea looks like!

529
00:32:19,570 --> 00:32:20,310
It's so pretty.

530
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:22,650
♫ How can one own a rainbow? ♫

531
00:32:22,730 --> 00:32:24,360
Why is it so soft under my feet?

532
00:32:25,420 --> 00:32:26,300
It's cold.

533
00:32:26,390 --> 00:32:29,510
♫ How can one embrace the summer wind? ♫

534
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:31,310
The weather is so nice.

535
00:32:32,190 --> 00:32:36,420
♫ Stars in the sky make fun
of the people below ♫

536
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:38,260
It's too cold.

537
00:32:38,350 --> 00:32:43,810
♫ For never understanding,
never feeling content ♫

538
00:32:54,460 --> 00:32:54,940
Bye!

539
00:32:55,030 --> 00:33:01,060
♫ When the wind sweeps a kite
into the sky ♫

540
00:33:01,140 --> 00:33:06,420
♫ I say a prayer and a blessing for you,
and I'm moved ♫

541
00:33:06,510 --> 00:33:12,980
♫ Finally, as your form vanishes
in a sea of people ♫

542
00:33:13,070 --> 00:33:18,740
♫ I realize the tears shed with a smile
are the ones that hurt the most ♫
